WEBVTT

00:00:01.50 --> 00:00:06.58
This is journey twenty nine of Hewn, the software factory: update project skills.

00:00:06.58 --> 00:00:11.34
Every project starts with skills copied from Greenlit, Hewn's skill library,

00:00:11.34 --> 00:00:15.17
and stage zero records the commit it copied in a skills lock.

00:00:15.17 --> 00:00:17.42
Greenlit keeps improving after that.

00:00:17.42 --> 00:00:21.69
This video shows an Owner seeing that a project's skills are behind,

00:00:21.69 --> 00:00:25.95
and bringing them up to date with a pull request that merges itself.

00:00:27.10 --> 00:00:31.26
When Greenlit's default branch is ahead of a project's skills lock,

00:00:31.26 --> 00:00:35.48
an Owner sees "Skills update available", with the number of commits.

00:00:35.48 --> 00:00:40.45
Choosing Update skills opens a pull request that updates the skill files and the

00:00:40.45 --> 00:00:43.62
lock, and it merges automatically when checks pass.

00:00:43.62 --> 00:00:44.86
Viewers see no link.

00:00:44.86 --> 00:00:49.90
This is for Owners, who keep each project's agents working with Greenlit's latest

00:00:49.90 --> 00:00:50.33
skills.

00:00:51.48 --> 00:00:54.95
Here a project's lock is three commits behind Greenlit.

00:00:54.95 --> 00:00:59.74
The project header shows the Owner "Skills update available, three commits".

00:00:59.74 --> 00:01:04.22
The dialog lists Greenlit's commits since the locked one, newest first,

00:01:04.22 --> 00:01:08.13
and says the running increment finishes on the current skills.

00:01:08.13 --> 00:01:10.15
The Owner chooses Update skills.

00:01:10.15 --> 00:01:12.86
In under a second the pull request is open,

00:01:12.86 --> 00:01:17.91
the toast says it merges automatically when checks pass, and the link goes away.

00:01:17.91 --> 00:01:21.63
About eight seconds after the click the checks have passed,

00:01:21.63 --> 00:01:26.68
the pull request has merged, and the lock on the default branch names Greenlit's

00:01:26.68 --> 00:01:26.99
head.

00:01:27.34 --> 00:01:32.68
When Greenlit can't be reached, the dialog says the skills weren't updated, and why.

00:01:32.68 --> 00:01:35.66
The project keeps running on the skills it has,

00:01:35.66 --> 00:01:38.33
and Try again sends the request once more.

00:01:39.48 --> 00:01:42.17
The design planned a worker run for this.

00:01:42.17 --> 00:01:47.30
But an update belongs to no direction and no stage, so the API does it itself,

00:01:47.30 --> 00:01:49.66
as the new decision record explains.

00:01:49.66 --> 00:01:53.14
The project page asks for the update only for Owners.

00:01:53.14 --> 00:01:57.48
The handler reads the lock from the repository, and asks Greenlit,

00:01:57.48 --> 00:02:02.80
through a bare git clone fetched at most once a minute, for the commits after it.

00:02:03.15 --> 00:02:08.66
Update skills commits Greenlit's skill files and the new lock to a branch named for

00:02:08.66 --> 00:02:11.58
Greenlit's head, and opens the pull request.

00:02:11.58 --> 00:02:14.96
Folders the project kept at bootstrap stay its own.

00:02:14.96 --> 00:02:20.01
The update is recorded, and an event tells Mission Control to read it again.

00:02:20.01 --> 00:02:22.26
Only one update is open at a time.

00:02:22.61 --> 00:02:25.80
A merger sweeps open updates every ten seconds.

00:02:25.80 --> 00:02:30.28
It waits while checks run, and merges once every check has passed.

00:02:30.28 --> 00:02:34.29
If the default branch moved, it puts the same files on top,

00:02:34.29 --> 00:02:35.98
and the checks run again.

00:02:35.98 --> 00:02:39.85
A failed check leaves the pull request open and unmerged,

00:02:39.85 --> 00:02:42.03
and the update is offered again.

00:02:42.38 --> 00:02:45.83
This sequence shows the whole path, from the link to the merge.

00:02:46.98 --> 00:02:49.74
The backend tests go through the real API,

00:02:49.74 --> 00:02:53.35
against a real git repository standing in for Greenlit.

00:02:53.35 --> 00:02:58.08
The update test opens the pull request and checks the branch, the title,

00:02:58.08 --> 00:03:02.21
the new skill files, the folder the project kept, and the lock.

00:03:02.21 --> 00:03:05.04
Asking again returns the same pull request.

00:03:05.04 --> 00:03:10.48
Other tests cover skills already up to date, an unreachable Greenlit, and a Viewer,

00:03:10.48 --> 00:03:11.60
who is forbidden.

00:03:11.95 --> 00:03:16.94
The merger tests merge once checks pass, rebase a branch that fell behind,

00:03:16.94 --> 00:03:18.83
and leave a failed one open.

00:03:18.83 --> 00:03:23.82
A repository with no CI at all reports no checks, so it would never merge.

00:03:23.82 --> 00:03:29.49
That test failed first, and now such an update merges once no check has appeared for

00:03:29.49 --> 00:03:30.30
two minutes.

00:03:30.30 --> 00:03:33.67
All three hundred and eighteen backend tests pass.

00:03:34.02 --> 00:03:38.43
End to end, a behaviour test commits to the e2e stack's own Greenlit,

00:03:38.43 --> 00:03:43.17
then updates the skills in Mission Control and waits for the lock to reach

00:03:43.17 --> 00:03:44.19
Greenlit's head.

00:03:44.19 --> 00:03:47.39
Other tests cover the failed state and the Viewer.

00:03:47.39 --> 00:03:52.13
Visual tests compare the link and the dialog with their mocks, by default,

00:03:52.13 --> 00:03:56.10
busy and failed, and an accessibility test checks every state.

00:03:57.25 --> 00:03:59.95
A Viewer sees the project with no link.

00:03:59.95 --> 00:04:03.75
The dialog reads the same in dark mode, and on a phone.

00:04:04.90 --> 00:04:07.09
Journey twenty nine is complete.

00:04:07.09 --> 00:04:10.91
Owners see when Greenlit is ahead of a project's skills.

00:04:10.91 --> 00:04:15.62
Update skills opens a pull request with the new skill files and lock.

00:04:15.62 --> 00:04:18.49
And it merges itself once its checks pass.

00:04:18.49 --> 00:04:20.26
Next comes journey thirty.
